      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand this last one. It won\u0027t be used most of the time, since a WHERE audit_id\u003d\u0027xxx\u0027 AND issued_before \u003e\u003d \u0027datething\u0027 will have to do the range query on issued_before, and won\u0027t be able to apply the audit_id at all. It\u0027s possible EXISTS queries will be able to do some magic there, so I could be wrong, but I\u0027d be interested to see EXPLAIN\u0027s, becuase I think the optimizer will favor range scanning the much smaller issued_before index in most cases.",
